Lab 7: Error Handling and Dead Letter Queues (DLQ) with Apache Camel
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Implement robust error handling mechanisms in Apache Camel routes using onException()
Configure retry logic with redelivery policies and exponential backoff
Create and configure Dead Letter Queues (DLQ) for failed message processing
Simulate various error scenarios to test error handling and DLQ routing behavior
Analyze failed messages in DLQ output to support troubleshooting and monitoring
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Apache Camel concepts (routes, endpoints, components)
Familiarity with Java programming fundamentals
Knowledge of the Maven build tool
Basic Linux command-line skills
This lab uses a self-contained, embedded ActiveMQ Artemis broker started in-process, so no external broker installation or network access is required. All work happens in an isolated local project directory.

Required tools and their installation (skip any step if the tool is already installed on your machine):

java -version
mvn -version
You need OpenJDK 11 (or later) and Maven 3.8+. If they are missing, install them with your distribution's package manager, for example:

sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y openjdk-11-jdk maven
